-- L/instanceof-constructor: `value instanceof make` with `make` an arrow function and `value` an
-- object. TypeScript accepts any function on the right, through Function's [Symbol.hasInstance];
-- V8 reads the right side's prototype only because the left side is an object, and throws.
⟨.instOf (.record []) (.lam .top (.var 0)), .bool,
  .instOfCallable (.record (τs := []) (by decide) (fun i => by cases i <;> rfl) (fun i l e τ h _ => by simp at h))
    (.lam (.var rfl)), rfl⟩
